From: Dana Fried <dfried@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:46:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] [Thumbnails] Prevent re-entrancy that leads to data
 corruption

Original change's description:
> [Thumbnails] Prevent re-entrancy that leads to data corruption
>
> This avoids a very edgy edge case where some variables were not updated
> before calling a method that could (again, in a very specific edge case)
> cause re-entrancy, which in turn could cause eventual data corruption.
>
> Fixed: 584069904
> Change-Id: Ib91856a88d7bfe0021459dcc9fb865ae937b148d
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8824290
> Reviewed-by: Muhammad Salmaan <musalmaan@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Dana Fried <dfried@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1745795}

(cherry picked from commit 7c903bac42ceb363fa36dbf3fdd819e51728e81a)

Bug: 587226645,584069904
Change-Id: Ib91856a88d7bfe0021459dcc9fb865ae937b148d
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8837880
Reviewed-by: David Pennington <dpenning@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Steven Luong <stluong@chromium.org>
